  "answer":"Your business risk assessment for NFTF activities should assess the risks associated with carrying on NFTF business, with particular focus on the use of eKYC Systems, and identify actions to mitigate those risks. [PID:31f0a7bd-a9fa-4aab-a4b4-32d0a6fb51b2]\n\nIt should reflect that different risks may arise when business is conducted entirely on an NFTF basis versus a mix of face-to-face and NFTF interactions. [PID:c24c6dfe-b5fa-4802-81ab-5894795d4362]\n\nIt should also assess Financial Crime risks linked to the technology, including heightened risks after onboarding (e.g., transaction fraud, money laundering, or theft of digitally stored CDD documentation), even if eKYC reduces impersonation risk at onboarding. [PID:06936741-ee7c-4307-b4eb-c86c1a6f83af]\n\nMitigation measures to consider/implement include adopting appropriate measures to mitigate eKYC risks by ensuring eKYC is secure and effective, uses an appropriate combination of authentication factors, is at least as stringent as face-to-face CDD, and verifies both the authenticity of government ID and the actual customer. [PID:aecde7ad-d719-4416-b520-a9e53a58934f]\n\nThe assessment should also reference/incorporate relevant mitigation measures recommended by the Regulator, competent U.A.E. authorities, FATF, and other relevant bodies. [PID:c24c6dfe-b5fa-4802-81ab-5894795d4362]",
